invariant: INV-14
file: srv_resume.c
catches: quic_loop_test
reason: the ticket walk holds each ticket to its own QUIC version rather
  than the session's, so a server that chose version 2 resumes a ticket
  issued in a version 1 connection, and a TCP server resumes a QUIC
  server's ticket. RFC 9369 section 5 has a server accept no ticket from
  another version and fall back to a full handshake
  (rfc9369.txt:276-281). test/quic_loop_ticket_versions.h requires a raw
  client's version 1 ticket to fail closed against a server that chose
  version 2, and test/srv_resume_tests.h, in bin/srv_flight_test,
  requires a TCP server to pass over a ticket that records version 1.

--- old
            ticket_holds(c, cfg, ch, sel, session_quic_version(t))) {
--- new
            ticket_holds(c, cfg, ch, sel, c->quic_version)) {
